   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing Tu Vien Truc Lam Buddhist Central, Inc. to\nfile an application for certain real property tax exemptions",
    "basePrintNo": "S8799",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8799-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8799\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing Tu Vien Truc Lam Buddhist Central,\nInc.  to file an application for certain real property tax exemptions\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAllows the not-for-profit corporation, Tu Vien Truc Lam Buddhist\nCentral, Inc. to file an application for exemption from real property\ntaxes with the Town of Brookhaven in relation to the sale of real prop-\nerty.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Authorizes the assessor for the Town of Brookhaven may accept\nan application for exemption from property taxes owed on the property\nlocated at 356 Terryville Road, Port Jefferson Station, New York 11776.\nUpon granting such exemption, the applicable governing tax department\nshall have discretion to exempt outstanding taxes owed.\n\nSection 2. Sets forth an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTu Vien Truc Lam Buddhist Central, Inc. is a not-for-profit- tax exempt\norganization that missed the tax exempt filling status due to a delayed\nclosing date during the sale of the property. They have requested retro-\nactive relief from property tax that would not apply to a non-profit.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTBD\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
